World pass integration (branch world-icons-pass): NOT APPLIED. It needs the owner's approval.

What it does: TycoonCore builds the world around the plots once, when the server starts, from WorldArt and
WorldVisuals. It passes its own PLOT_SPACING, MAX_PLOTS and plotCenter, so the world moves with the plots if
those ever change. Both modules are required inside pcall with a 5 second wait, the same way as PlotVisuals and
PlotArt: if either is missing or broken there is one warning and the game runs exactly as today. No save, no
remote, no player data, no touch handler, nothing runs per player.

The two edits, in TycoonCore.lua at main e3c9e67 (TycoonCore is the only file this changes):
  E1  after line 61 (the end of the "Plot visuals are off" block, lines 56-61): 10 lines that require
      WorldVisuals and WorldArt inside pcall and warn if they are missing.
  E2  between line 839 (the end of onPlayerAdded) and line 840 (Players.PlayerAdded:Connect(onPlayerAdded)):
      12 lines that build the world once inside pcall, from PLOT_SPACING (line 74), MAX_PLOTS (line 76) and
      plotCenter (lines 123-126).

Studio steps by hand, in this order (nothing syncs by itself):
  1. ServerScriptService: create a ModuleScript named exactly WorldArt and paste WorldArt.lua into it.
  2. ServerScriptService: create a ModuleScript named exactly WorldVisuals and paste WorldVisuals.lua into it.
     Do both before pasting TycoonCore (it waits 5 s for each inside pcall, so it never hangs, but without
     them the world is simply not built).
  3. Only after approval: apply this patch (git apply docs/world_pass_integration.patch on a branch that claims
     TycoonCore), then paste the new TycoonCore.lua into the Script TycoonCore (ServerScriptService).
  4. Delete Workspace.PREVIEW_WORLD if it exists (the preview would lie on top of the real world), then F5.
  5. View > Drafts: commit every draft. Publish with Shut down all servers, as always.

Checked by tools/world_test.py --integration: the patch applies to main's TycoonCore.lua, the patched file
passes tools/daily_test.py and tools/world_test.py, and the two inserted blocks build the world in the fake.

--- a/TycoonCore.lua
+++ b/TycoonCore.lua
@@ -60,6 +60,16 @@ if not (visualsOk and artOk) then
 	PlotVisuals, PlotArt = nil, nil
 end
 
+-- The world around the plots (the spawn plaza, paths to every plot, lamps, trees, a street sign per plot):
+-- WorldVisuals builds it from the data in WorldArt (both in ServerScriptService). Only looks, never saved.
+-- Loaded inside pcall: if either is missing or broken, the game runs as before on the bare Baseplate.
+local worldVisualsOk, WorldVisuals = pcall(require, script.Parent:WaitForChild("WorldVisuals", 5))
+local worldArtOk, WorldArt = pcall(require, script.Parent:WaitForChild("WorldArt", 5))
+if not (worldVisualsOk and worldArtOk) then
+	warn("World visuals are off: " .. tostring(worldVisualsOk and WorldArt or WorldVisuals))
+	WorldVisuals, WorldArt = nil, nil
+end
+
 -- Upgrades are bought in this order, in the shop's Office tab (ShopClient). cost = Cash, income = Cash per second.
 -- icon is only for that tab.
 local UPGRADES = {
@@ -837,6 +847,18 @@ local function onPlayerAdded(player)
 		task.spawn(teleportToPlot, player.Character, slot)
 	end
 end
+
+-- The world around the plots, built once from this script's own plot numbers (a new PLOT_SPACING or MAX_PLOTS
+-- moves it with the plots). Looks only: if it fails, a warning, and the game runs without it.
+if WorldVisuals then
+	local worldOk, worldError = pcall(function()
+		WorldVisuals.build(workspace, WorldArt, WorldVisuals.site(WorldArt, PLOT_SPACING, MAX_PLOTS, plotCenter))
+	end)
+	if not worldOk then
+		warn("World visuals: the world could not be built: " .. tostring(worldError))
+	end
+end
+
 Players.PlayerAdded:Connect(onPlayerAdded)
 -- Players already in the server (they joined while this script was still starting) are set up too
